The `tile` pointer advances by `sizeof(QRgb)` = 4 bytes per pixel. For `width * height` pixels, it advances by `width * height * 4` bytes. The buffer is 16384 bytes. So if `width * height > 4096`, the `tile` pointer would go past the end of the buffer.

But `width` and `height` are the dimensions of the QImage, which were set in `composeTiles` to at most 64. So `width * height <= 4096`.

